<title>INDIA: India's EIH 1996/97 net higher.</title>
<headline>India's EIH 1996/97 net higher.</headline>
<dateline>BOMBAY 1997-06-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>Year to March 31, 1997.</p>
<p>	     (in million rupees unless stated)</p>
<p>    Net profit		1,381.2  vs  1,201.60</p>
<p>    Net sales		 4,404.20 vs  3,956.30</p>
<p>    Shr (in rupees)	    35.29 vs   35.55</p>
<p>    Div (in rupees)	     5.0  vs    4.5</p>
<p>    Other income		290.60 vs    256.40</p>
<p>    Expenditure	     2,873.40 vs  2,475.90</p>
<p>    Interest		    123.20 vs    159.10</p>
<p>    Gross profit	    1,698.20 vs  1,577.70</p>
<p>    Depreciation		156.70 vs    134.60</p>
<p>    Taxation		    160.30 vs    241.50</p>
<p>Note: Leading hospitality firm EIH Limited said the earnings per share had been worked out an expanded share capital.</p>
<p>The company allotted 1,125,114 equity shares on November 6 in response to an option exercised by holders of detachable warrants issued along with its 16 percent non-covertible debenture issue.</p>
<p>EIH issued 17,484,299 equity shares as fully paid bonus shares last December by capitalising part of the share premium account.</p>
<p>-- Bombay newsroom +91-22-265 9000</p>
</text>
